//   1  a completed answer's edit (answer - its input) stored in the anchor's coordinates
//   2  a rebuilt frame: the last answer's edit carried along the game's vectors onto this frame
//   3  the fill: pixels the carried edit cannot be trusted on (just uncovered) take it from trusted pixels nearby
// Bit 134217728 of `protection` shows mode 2's decisions instead of the picture (direct, uncovered, donor mass).
// The two-sided rebuild: `side` 1 = mode 2 stores (edit, trust) into Side0 instead of the picture, `side` 2 merges its
// own with them into Side0 (merge_sides); mode 4 = the forward field (where this frame's pixels are in the NEXT frame) by
// inverting the next frame's backward vectors; mode 3 with side 3 fills from Side0.
// Two-sided rebuild with rebuild_flags & 2: mode 2 weighs each side by its outline context (context.comp's classes of this
// frame's depth and of the anchors' depths), carried in MatchOut0 / in side 2's registers; the merge applies the weights.
// Mode 7 = this frame's depth at every pixel (depth_at, the bilinear read of Depth) into DepthFullOut: modes 6, 2 and 3
// read a pixel's depth from it instead of filtering again - run first. Mode 6 = the nearer surface near each pixel of the
// frame (its depth alone decides it: the same for both sides) into PickOut, read by mode 2 - run before it.
