// beside it - is still next to its source: the answer's own edge profile there holds its edit. The wide donors (a grid
// step away, weighted by the coarse depth) gave such pixels the other surface's edit - with Legacy 3's edits (a lit pane
// +100 codes, the post in front of it -40) a notch along the edge on every rebuilt frame. They are taken as far as their
// colours match (their absolute mass); where they do not (a surface just uncovered, a colour not near the source) the
// wide donors decide. A long vector's end is no pixel-exact source (motion blur along it): they fade out from 40 to 80 px
